    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "The Pacific Plate is the largest exclusively oceanic plate and forms the highly active Circum-Pacific Belt ('Ring of Fire').",
        "Divergent boundaries create new crust at mid-ocean ridges, while convergent boundaries destroy crust through subduction.",
        "Transform boundaries involve horizontal sliding of plates past one another without creating or destroying crust."
      ],
